<!-- WHERE IT SENDS YOU -->
<section class="wrap chapter" id="onward" aria-labelledby="h-on">
  <div class="lens-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Where it sends you</p>
    <h2 id="h-on">A front door that points onward</h2>
    <p>I want a front door to send people onward: to the right owner, the right page for their role and the right next step.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="scrolly">
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step" data-step="0" id="s-on-0"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Link to the source</p>
        <h3>Owners keep their own content</h3>
        <p>The front door links to guidance its owners maintain instead of copying it, so each owner keeps their own content current.</p>
        <p data-aud="pro">The single-source principle: one canonical owner for each piece of guidance, linked rather than copied.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="1" id="s-on-1"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">Role-based next steps</p>
        <h3>Start from your role</h3>
        <p>Each role gets one page that points to what applies to it, and everyone gets a “start here”.</p>
      </div></div>
      <div class="step" data-step="2" id="s-on-2"><div class="step-in">
        <p class="kicker">From principle to action</p>
        <h3>Every principle ends in a next step</h3>
        <p>A page that states a principle ends with what it means for you, what to do, and who to ask, so nobody reaches a dead end at "be responsible".</p>
      </div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="graphic">
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="sec dim" data-on="0">
          <span class="lab">Link, don't copy</span>
